 "not_modelled": [
  "Peer data is not retransmitted in a time-slotted schedule: capacity is shared by strict priority per step, and the Shannon bound is an upper bound, so throughput is too and the energy per bit a lower bound. No LTE or 5G modulation and coding table is applied.",
  "A helper's charge falls only by the forwarding energy counted here: its own loads and its solar charging are not modelled, so a charge cut-off is reached later than it would be in flight.",
  "Receive and idle-listening power, wake-up and discovery signalling, and handshake time.",
  "The Earth-uplink energy and rate of an exit node are counted only if its uplink figures are entered; otherwise its uplink is taken as neither limiting nor costing energy.",
  "Data buffered in a helper that is no longer on any route is not drained.",
  "Ground reflection off the actual terrain: the two-ray model reflects from one flat plane of the stated permittivity at the antennas' common height reference; rough or sloping ground, rocks and diffraction past a ridge are not in the loss (a ridge that blocks the path blocks the link).",
  "Delay-tolerant bundle handling (custody, retransmission, expiry): data is moved or dropped by the buffer rule only; light-time and queueing delay are not computed.",
  "Rover motion between waypoints: a node sits at each waypoint until the next.",
  "Interference between nodes and the lander's antenna pattern; antennas are isotropic with the entered gain at both ends."
 ],
